====technology_choice
The practical rule: If more than 50% of your app is genuinely shareable
business logic (networking, data, validation), KMP pays for its setup cost.
Below that threshold, the shared module overhead doesn’t earn back its
maintenance cost. If your app is mostly UI with minimal shared logic, Flutter
or native is a better option.

Don’t forget about the hiring factor. Kotlin developers can contribute to KMP
projects right away. Flutter requires Dart expertise, which is a smaller talent
pool.

